From a104be87142cd60cc3a42195d5d6d710325a39ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:14:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(web-scan): report recheck overflow at save, rescan
 from the lowest owed block, pin carry filters

Review of b439faf on #70:

- M1: the overflow of a truncated recheck list is now reported through
  onProgress right after the save that persisted it
  (ScanProgress.recheckOverflow), and the Scan view sets its recheck
  notice from progress as well as from the result, so a later failure in
  the same run no longer hides it.
- M2: RecheckOverflow.fromBlock is now the lowest owed block of the whole
  set (the first kept block), not the first dropped one. A rescan typed
  from it starts without the stored list, so its main scan re-reads every
  kept and dropped claim; the old block lost the 8 kept payments. The
  "Rescan from block {block}" copy is unchanged and now covers all of them.
- M3: pins the '< saved.nextBlock' carry filter (a replay-tail claim is
  left to the main re-scan; carrying it would also make the stored list
  invalid on load).
- Tests pin the RECHECK_MAX cap on a passed-in cursor (11 valid blocks,
  exactly 8 single-block reads), the router-caller filter of the recheck
  pass and its maxMatchesPerScan guard (reachable; kept).
- withOwedRechecks JSDoc documents the accepted re-retry when a run saves
  no checkpoint and the silent drops of the recheck pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
